# The repository has core.autocrlf=true on Windows checkouts, which would give
# .nvmrc a CRLF ending locally. nvm / nvm-windows read the file literally and
# choke on the trailing \r, so the Node standard would silently fail to apply
# for Windows developers. GitHub Actions' setup-node is unaffected (Linux
# runners always see LF), so this is purely a local-developer guard.
.nvmrc text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for shell scripts: CI executes .github/sql-ci/run.sh on a
# Linux runner, and a CRLF checkout committed from Windows would fail at the
# shebang with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" — a confusing failure a
# long way from its cause. Git's autocrlf already normalises on commit; this
# makes it explicit rather than dependent on each contributor's config.
*.sh text eol=lf
